# ── What the admin passcode is ────────────────────────────────

[admin_warning.title]
This code is the whole machine

[admin_warning.grants]
The admin passcode gives whoever holds it unrestricted access to this computer:
every screen, the mouse and the keyboard, with no approval asked for anything.

[admin_warning.unattended]
With unattended access installed that includes the lock screen and administrator
prompts — the things a password would normally stop.

[admin_warning.sharing]
Keep it for your own devices, and send it somewhere private if you must send it
at all — not a group chat, not a screen share. Anything that ends up holding it
is you, as far as this machine is concerned.

[admin_warning.mitigations]
Two things soften a mistake. The first connection from each new device has to be
approved here, so a code that gets out cannot be used behind your back. And the
reset button beside the code revokes it — along with every device it has already
let in.

[admin_warning.understood]
I understand


