# ── What the quality/latency slider is doing ──────────────────

[priority.quality]
Holds the picture. If the link or the hardware falls behind, the frame rate
drops before the resolution does, and sound is buffered generously so it stays
continuous.

[priority.balanced]
Balanced. Trouble is answered with bitrate first, then whichever of detail and
smoothness is cheaper to give up.

[priority.responsive]
Favours responsiveness. Resolution softens before the frame rate is allowed to
fall.

[priority.latency]
Holds the frame rate. Detail is spent freely, and sound is buffered as little as
possible, to keep everything immediate.


